## 3. The Eta9 Theta Series Fixes the Orientation

Let `tau=zeta_3` and put

\[
 q=\exp(2\pi i\tau/6),\qquad
 \widetilde w=\exp(2\pi i(z+(1-\tau)/2)).
\]

The modified level-three theta basis is

\[
 \vartheta_k(z)=\sum_{m\in\mathbb Z}
 q^{(3m+k)^2}\widetilde w^{3m+k},
 \qquad k=0,1,2.                                      \tag{1}
\]

Set `omega=exp(2*pi*i/3)`. Directly in (1), translation by the two marked
three-torsion generators gives

\[
 \vartheta_k(z+1/3)=\omega^k\vartheta_k(z),             \tag{2}
\]

and, after replacing `3m+k` by `3m+k+1`,

\[
 \vartheta_k(z+\tau/3)
 =q^{-1}\widetilde w^{-1}\vartheta_{k+1}(z).            \tag{3}
\]

The factor in (3) is independent of `k`, so it is projectively irrelevant.
On the value vector `vartheta=(vartheta_0,vartheta_1,vartheta_2)^t`, define

\[
 X(v_0,v_1,v_2)^t=(v_1,v_2,v_0)^t,
 \qquad Z=\operatorname{diag}(1,\omega,\omega^2).
\]

Equations (2)-(3) give `XZ=omega ZX`. With the ordered marking

```text
first coordinate a  = tau/3 (the u_B direction),
second coordinate b = 1/3   (the u_A direction),
```

put `U_(a,b)=X^a Z^b`. Then

\[
 U_{(a,b)}U_{(c,d)}
 =\omega^{-cb}U_{(a+c,b+d)}.                            \tag{4}
\]

Thus the eta9 theta series realizes exactly the selected `m=1` cocycle from
`UST.G3AA`, including its orientation. It is not merely an unspecified
generator of an abstract `Z3`.

The exact Hesse-to-Fermat change of basis used by eta9 conjugates every `U_g`
by one invertible matrix. It therefore leaves (4) unchanged. The theta and
frozen Fermat descriptions carry the same projective representation.

